{
  "what_this_is": "The MoE thesis, measured. docs/MINING.md's first open surface was 'a model with less weight traffic per token', because the persist ceiling is 2*min(capacity, footprint)/step_traffic and the capacity is fixed by the device. Qwen3.6-35B-A3B is the same architecture family, the same runtime, the same hook and the same box as the dense Qwen3.8-27B matrix in rtx5090-baseline-matrix.json - with a sparse MoE FFN reading 8 of 256 experts per token. Every number here is a control/candidate pair measured minutes apart on one RTX 5090.",
  "model": {
    "label": "Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, unsloth UD-Q4_K_M GGUF, 22.1 GB",
    "architecture": "sparse-MoE hybrid Gated-DeltaNet / full attention",
    "repository": "unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF",
    "file": "Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-Q4_K_M.gguf",
    "_geometry_source": "read from the GGUF's own metadata and tensor shapes, not from the runtime's defaults: block_count 40, full_attention_interval 4 (so 30 recurrent layers, confirmed by which blocks carry ssm_* tensors), ssm.state_size 128, ssm.group_count 16 (linear_q_heads), blk.0.attn_qkv.weight [2048, 8192] so linear_qkvdim 8192 and linear_v_heads (8192 - 2*16*128)/128 = 32, ssm.conv_kernel 4.",
    "num_hidden_layers": 40,
    "full_attention_interval": 4,
    "recurrent_layers": 30,
    "linear_num_value_heads": 32,
    "linear_key_head_dim": 128,
    "linear_conv_kernel_dim": 4,
    "lin_state_bytes_per_layer": 2097152,
    "lin_conv_state_bytes_per_layer": 49152,
    "_state_formulas": "lin_state = linear_v_heads * linear_head_dim^2 * sizeof(float) (qwen35.cpp:560); lin_conv = (linear_conv_kernel-1) * linear_qkvdim * sizeof(bf16) (qwen35.cpp:559). Both formulas reproduce the pinned Qwen3.8-27B numbers exactly.",
    "n_experts": 256,
    "experts_used_per_token": 8
  },
