  "how_to_reproduce": {
    "model": "hf download unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-Q4_K_M.gguf",
    "build": "integrations/sparkinfer/build.sh $WORK   # the same pinned commit; the hook is model-independent, it brackets whatever the runtime marks as a linear attention layer",
    "sweep": "eval/real_sweep.py --binary $W/qwen3_gguf_bench --model $MODEL.gguf --axis mode --repeats 3 --warmup-runs 1 --fixed RECURLOCAL_STATS=1 RECURLOCAL_WINDOW_ATTACH=capture_node",
    "why_capture_node": "production decode is a captured CUDA graph and a stream access-policy window is host-side state capture never records, so without it the persist family defers every window and applies no policy at all"
  },
  "the_runtime_stops_batching_above_eight_rows": {
    "what": "At its default packed-row cap this runtime stops batching above 8 rows. At 16 and 32 sequences it packed 127 of 2173 and 127 of 4205 tokens and decoded the rest one row at a time, which is why aggregate throughput at both is ~455 tok/s - BELOW the 503 tok/s single-sequence rate, and 5.4x below the 2456 tok/s it reaches at 8 rows.",
    "cause": "launch_mmvq_q4k_rows refuses M > 8 (kernels/csrc/cuda/gemm/gemv.cu) and the bf16 launch_mmvq_rows dispatcher has no chunking loop, unlike its own _f32 sibling which chunks M into groups of 8. So the first Q4_K projection of a wider batch is refused, dflash_verify_short_run declines at layer 0, and decode_packed returns false for the whole batch. The runtime says so itself: '[dflash-verify] mmvq_rows refused type=12 N=16 n_out=8192 K=2048' followed by '[dflash-verify] declined at layer=0'.",
    "proof": "The engine already splits a batch wider than its packed-row cap into chunks of that cap, and the cap is an environment variable, so setting it to the width the GEMV accepts isolates the cause with nothing else changed. With SPARKINFER_PACKED_MAX_ROWS=8: concurrency 16 goes from 5.8% packed at 452.8 tok/s to 94.4% at 1204.4, and concurrency 32 from 3.0% at 455.6 to 97.3% at 1226.8. The cliff is 5.4x (8 rows vs 16 at the default cap); the cap recovers 2.7x of it, not all, because chunking re-reads the weights once per chunk.",
    "consequence_for_this_matrix": "every arm marked runtime_row_cap 8 was measured with the cap set on BOTH arms - it is a property of the workload, not of the candidate. Any arm still marked 'default (32)' at 16 or 32 sequences is recorded because it was measured, not because it means what its label says; eval/real_eval.py now refuses such an arm by name.",
    "whose_bug": "SparkInfer's, not RecurLocal's. It is the surface docs/MINING.md lists third, and it is worth two orders of magnitude more than anything this library does."
  },
  "provenance": {
    "gpu": "NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5090, sm_120, 32 GB, 170 SMs, 1792 GB/s",
    "cuda": "13.3",
    "runtime": "SparkInfer 5347b27c (the pinned commit)",
    "model": "unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF, Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-Q4_K_M.gguf, 22.13 GB",
    "note": "One box for every arm. Graphics clocks cannot be pinned in this container, so only same-box interleaved deltas are trustworthy."
  }
